INCORPORATED SOURCES — already in the public domain
---------------------------------------------------

The biblical texts, lexicons, and cross-reference apparatus this work
builds on were ALREADY in the public domain before incorporation —
either by age or by their creators' own dedication — and remain so.
They are NOT the subject of the CC0 dedication above (one cannot
dedicate what one does not own); they are simply public-domain material
reused here. Per-source provenance is documented in `COPYRIGHT.md` and,
for each translation, in `content/translations/<id>/_meta.yaml`. In
brief:

  - World English Bible (WEB) — dedicated to the public domain by
    Rainbow Missions, Inc.
  - Strong's Hebrew & Greek lexicons (James Strong, 1890) — PD by age.
  - Treasury of Scripture Knowledge (R. A. Torrey, 1834) — PD by age.
  - Douay-Rheims, Clementine Vulgate, JPS 1917, Van Dyck Arabic,
    Westminster Leningrad Codex, Swete LXX, Byzantine Majority Text —
    public domain by age and/or their own dedication; see COPYRIGHT.md
    for per-source detail.


